{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'append\"'!|transaction'\"' src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc; sed -n '1,90p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py; printenv CODEX_THREAD_ID; command -v bb; command -v clojure; command -v python3\"","aggregated_output":"8:   (dao.stream.md, Composition): append!/transact! allocate transaction time\n9:   and write transaction records through the local stream's writer surface,\n28:   The transactor owns transaction time. Every append! or transact! writes\n29:   exactly ONE atomic transaction record to the local stream\n31:     {:dao.space/transaction {:t <nonnegative-integer> :datoms [...]}}\n34:   transaction. t is allocated from a per-value watermark: on create! the\n57:  \"One datom per k/v pair, all sharing transaction time `t`. `:db/id` is\n76:   transaction time: a non-nil explicit t is rejected, a nil t is stamped\n84:          \"the transactor owns transaction time: explicit datom t is rejected\"\n118:  \"Derive the next transaction time from a flattened retained history: 0 for\n135:  \"Append one atomic transaction record to the local stream. The answer is\n144:  (let [record {:dao.space/transaction {:t t, :datoms datoms}}\n145:        answer (stream/append! local-stream record)]\n146:    (if-not (stream/valid-outcome? :append! answer)\n181:          \"the transactor derives transaction time from retained history; :next-t is not accepted\"\n209:(defn append!\n210:  \"Append one entity map or datom vector as a single atomic transaction.\n227:              (throw (ex-info \"append! produced no datoms\" {:val val})))\n233:  single atomic transaction: every datom shares one allocated t and lands\n234:  in one transaction record through exactly one local append, so no partial\n242:    (throw (ex-info \"transact! requires at least one transaction item\"\n258:  \"Close this transactor value: further append!/transact! answer\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nPR Reviewer Utility Script for Git-based Code Reviews.\nParses git diffs, analyzes churn and file risk categories, scans for security smells\nand debugging code, and produces structured markdown or JSON review reports.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Finding:\n    severity: str  # P0 (Critical), P1 (High), P2 (Medium), P3 (Low)\n    category: str  # Security, Debug, Quality, ErrorHandling, TestCoverage\n    file_path: str\n    line_number: Optional[int]\n    message: str\n    snippet: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass FileStat:\n    path: str\n    additions: int\n    deletions: int\n    category: str\n    risk_level: str  # High, Medium, Low\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ReviewSummary:\n    target: str\n    total_files: int\n    total_additions: int\n    total_deletions: int\n    test_additions: int\n    source_additions: int\n    test_to_source_ratio: float\n    file_stats: List[FileStat] = field(default_factory=list)\n    findings: List[Finding] = field(default_factory=list)\n    commits: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n\ndef run_git_command(args: List[str], cwd: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Helper to run git commands cleanly.\"\"\"\n    cmd = [\"git\"] + args\n    try:\n        res = subprocess.run(\n            cmd,\n            cwd=cwd,\n            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n            stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n            text=True,\n            check=True,\n        )\n        return res.stdout.strip()\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n        sys.stderr.write(f\"Git command failed: {' '.join(cmd)}\\nError: {e.stderr}\\n\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Git execution failed: {e.stderr.strip()}\")\n\n\ndef categorize_file(file_path: str) -> Tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Categorizes file type and assigns risk level.\"\"\"\n    path_lower = file_path.lower()\n\n    # Security & Auth\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"auth\", \"secret\", \"crypto\", \"token\", \"permission\", \"jwt\", \"oauth\", \"password\"]):\n        return \"Security/Auth\", \"High\"\n\n    # Database & Schema\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"migration\", \"schema\", \".sql\", \"entity\", \"db/\"]):\n        return \"Database/Schema\", \"High\"\n\n    # Infrastructure & Config\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"docker\", \"terraform\", \".tf\", \".env\", \"k8s\", \"helm\", \"ci/cd\", \".github/workflows\"]):\n        return \"Infra/Config\", \"High\"\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\"package.json\", \"deps.edn\", \"Cargo.toml\", \"go.mod\", \"requirements.txt\", \"pom.xml\", \"build.gradle\"]):\n        return \"Dependencies\", \"Medium\"\n\n    # API / Interfaces\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"proto\", \"openapi\", \"swagger\", \"graphql\", \"router\", \"controller\", \"api/\"]):\n        return \"API/Contract\", \"Medium\"\n01a099f1-87d6-7811-8a69-b3336b956fac\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/babashka/1.13.219/bb\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/clojure/1.12.4.1602/bin/clojure\n/usr/bin/python3\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
