{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md | sed -n '665,739p'; rg --files src/cljc/dao/data | head -12; sed -n '15,40p' src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   665\t\n   666\t### 4.1 The expansion event\n   667\t\n   668\tEvery attempt, successful or not, produces one event; so does every batch\n   669\trejected at admission. Events and the `m`-tagged output are appended to the\n   670\t**log** medium, when the expander has one; `program-out` receives only\n   671\tprogram.\n   672\t\n   673\t```\n   674\t[ev :yin/type           :macro-expand-event  t default-op]\n   675\t[ev :yin/source-batch   <ctx :t>             t default-op]   ; which source batch; always present\n   676\t[ev :yin/source-call    <call-eid>           t default-op]   ; eid in that batch, or in the log copy of the enclosing expansion; absent on an admission failure\n   677\t[ev :yin/macro-name     <sym>                t default-op]   ; when the operator was a :variable; absent for an inline macro lambda or an admission failure\n   678\t[ev :yin/macro          <lambda-eid>         t default-op]   ; only when durable (§4.2)\n   679\t[ev :yin/expansion-root <root'>              t default-op]   ; on success; names the LOG copy\n   680\t[ev :yin/error          {:kind ...}          t default-op]   ; on failure; plain data naming entities, never carrying input values\n   681\t[ev :yin/timestamp      <ctx :t>             t default-op]   ; logical, never a host clock\n   682\t```\n   683\t\n   684\tAn **admission-failure event** is the same entity with only `:yin/type`,\n   685\t`:yin/source-batch`, `:yin/error`, and `:yin/timestamp`: the batch had no\n   686\tusable call or macro to name. It is allocated from `:alloc`'s watermark\n   687\t(which needs no index), so a corrupt batch still produces exactly one\n   688\tplain-data event, advances `:ctx` once, and is retried through the same\n   689\tper-medium staging as any other log payload — never regenerated.\n   690\t\n   691\tThe log copy of expansion output carries `m = ev`; log copies of unchanged\n   692\toperands and ancestors carry `m = default-op` (re-parenting, not macro\n   693\toutput). **`program-out` datoms all carry `default-op`**: `m = ev` would be\n   694\ta cross-medium ref (§4.2). A nested expansion's `:yin/source-call` names a\n   695\tnode in the log copy of the enclosing expansion's output, which is how the\n   696\tchain source → event → root → event → root is walked for generated syntax.\n   697\t\"Every datom this expansion produced\" is `[?d _ _ _ ?ev]` on the log.\n   698\t\n   699\t`yin.vm.macro/event-schema` declares these attributes (`:yin/source-call`,\n   700\t`:yin/macro`, `:yin/expansion-root` as refs) for compositions that commit a\n   701\tlog to `dao.space`; the transactor relocates only declared refs, so a\n   702\tcomposition merges this fragment with `yin.vm/schema` before committing.\n   703\t\n   704\t### 4.2 Identity across media\n   705\t\n   706\t`program-in`, `program-out`, and the log are different media. A ref written\n   707\ton one that names an entity on another is meaningful only when the named\n   708\tid is **durable** — a permanent positive id from a committed stream. The\n   709\ttransactor (`dao.space.transact`) resolves tempids within one transaction;\n   710\tcommitting two batches separately does not connect them. Therefore:\n   711\t\n   712\t- `program-out` batches are self-contained: unchanged subtrees are copied,\n   713\t  with fresh ids, not referenced (decision 8).\n   714\t- `:yin/source-call` on an event names the call's eid *as it appeared in\n   715\t  the source batch*, qualified by `:yin/source-batch`; it is descriptive\n   716\t  until both media are committed under one resolution. `:yin/macro` is\n   717\t  written only when the macro's id is durable; otherwise `:yin/macro-name`\n   718\t  carries the name. Names are metadata, never identity repair.\n   719\t- `:yin/expansion-root` names the **log copy** of the output. The executed\n   720\t  program on `program-out` is a distinct copy with distinct ids; this design\n   721\t  promises no id-level correspondence between them. A composition that needs\n   722\t  one commits program and log in one transaction (they are one batch to the\n   723\t  transactor) or records the mapping itself.\n   724\t- A pipeline that wants queryable provenance commits `program-in` first and\n   725\t  expands against durable ids — the ordering rule of\n   726\t  `cross-language-macro.md` §4, retained. `ADR 0003` makes `dao.space` the\n   727\t  medium for that commit.\n   728\t\n   729\t### 4.3 Authority\n   730\t\n   731\tWrite authority on a medium is the whole model. Defining a macro is\n   732\tappending a definition to `program-in`; running a program is appending to\n   733\t`program-out`; both are decided by whoever holds the writer, and\n   734\t`dao.stream.md` puts that decision in the composition. A Shibi\n   735\tcapability, when it exists, is verified at the medium's boundary before the\n   736\tappend, not inside any VM. The old `:macro-authorize` VM option is gone\n   737\tbecause there is nothing left inside a VM to authorize.\n   738\t\n   739\t---\nsrc/cljc/dao/data/arrays.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\n  Comparators are caller-supplied; this namespace knows nothing of datoms.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude\n                  [conj disj count contains? seq rseq comparator sorted-set-by])\n  (:require #?(:cljd [\"dart:core\" :as dc])\n            [dao.data.arrays :as arr]))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Sentinels (§3.3.2) — two distinct empty arrays, compared by identity only.\n\n(def UNCHANGED\n  \"Returned by node-conj/node-disj when the key was already present/absent.\"\n  (arr/anew 0))\n\n\n(def EARLY-EXIT\n  \"Returned when a transient edited in place, nothing to propagate upward.\n   Unreachable in Phase 1 (edit lease is always nil).\"\n  (arr/anew 0))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Settings (§3.1)\n\n(def ^:private default-ref-type\n  ;; §5.3: :soft on the JVM (memory-pressure-aware), :strong on cljs/cljd\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
